BRUNEI DARUSSALAM STATISTICAL YEARBOOK 2025 BRUNEI DARUSSALAM STATISTICAL YEARBOOK 2025
Explanatory Note
POPULATION AND VITAL STATISTICS
1
Race
Race Group is divided into 3 main categories namely Malay, Chinese and Other Races.
Brunei Malay consists of the following indigenous groups of the Malay race, namely Brunei, Tutong, Belait, Kedayan, Dusun, Bisaya and Murut as
defined under the Brunei Nationality Act 1961.
Chinese refers to population who belong to the Chinese ethnic group. Meanwhile, the Other Races category consists of the remaining population not
included in the Malay and Chinese groups.
Average Annual Growth Rate
r = In(Pn/Po)/n where
     r is the average annual rate of growth
     n is the exact number of years between  Po and Pn
     Po is the population at the initial year
     Pn is the population at the later year
Population Density
Population Density refers to the density of persons per square kilometer. It is the ratio of the population of a given geographic area to the number of
square kilometres of the same area.
Sex Ratio
Sex Ratio refers to number of males per 1,000 females.
Residential Status
Residential Status is the status of the person in relation to the immigration laws of the country. The categories of residential status are :
 i) Brunei citizen, i.e. holder of Brunei Darussalam yellow identity card;
 ii) Permanent resident, i.e. holder of Brunei Darussalam purple identity card; and
 iii) Temporary resident, i.e. holder of Brunei Darussalam green identity card
Rate of Natural Increase
Rate of Natural Increase =             (No. of live births – No. of deaths) in year t
                                                            ------------------------------------------------------------            x 1,000
                 Mid-year population in year t
Birth Rate
Birth Rate =         No. of live births in year t
