Nota Keterangan
5
IMBANGAN PEMBAYARAN
Perangkaan Imbangan Pembayaran (BOP) meringkaskan transaksi ekonomi antara residen Negara Brunei Darussalam dan bukan residen. Perangkaan
BOP menyediakan satu rangka kerja bersepadu untuk penganalisaan ekonomi bagi hubungan ekonomi antarabangsa, ini termasuk prestasi ekonomi
antarabangsa Negara Brunei Darussalam, dasar kadar pertukaran, pengurusan rizab dan pendedahan luaran.
BOP Negara Brunei Darussalam dikumpul mengikut piawaian antarabangsa yang ditetapkan dalam garispandu Balance of Payments Manual, Sixth
Edition yang diterbitkan oleh Tabung Kewangan Antarabangsa (IMF). Transaksi ekonomi termasuk:
 • Transaksi eksport dan import barangan dan perkhidmatan
 • Transaksi pendapatan utama kepada jumlah yang dibayar dan diterima dalam pulangan untuk meneydiakan penggunaan
  sementara kepada entity pekerja lain, sumber kewangan atau bukan pengeluar bukan kewangan asset;
 • Transaksi pendapatan sekunder menengah yang menunjukkan pengagihan semula pendapatan; dan
 • Perolehan dan pelupusan asset dan liabiliti kewangan
BOP terdiri daripada 3 akaun utama:
 1. Akaun Semasa = Barangan + Perkhidmatan + Pendapatan Utama + Pendapatan Sekunder,
 2. Akaun Modal
 3. Akaun Kewangan= Perolehan dan pelupusan asset + liabiliti kewangan
Transaksi antarabangsa direkodkan dalam imbangan pembayaran adalah berdasarkan prinsip catatan bergu digunakan dalam perakaunan perniagaan,
di mana setiap transaksi terdapat dua penyertaan pengimbangan dengan nilai yang sama iaitu prinsip kredit dan debit yang sentiasa seimbang.
Explanatory Note
5
BALANCE OF PAYMENTS
Balance of Payments (BOP) statistics summarises the economic transactions between residents of Brunei Darussalam and non-residents. The BOP
statistics provide an integrated framework for the analysis of an economy’s international economic relationship, including Brunei Darussalam’s
international economic performance, exchange rate policy, reserve management and external vulnerability.
Brunei Darussalam’s BOP has been compiled in accordance with international standards set out in the Balance of Payments Manual, Sixth Edition
published by the International Monetary Fund (IMF). The economic transactions include:
 • transactions of exports and imports of goods and services;
 • transactions of primary income on the amount of payable and receivable in return for providing temporary use to another entity
  of labour, financial resources or nonproduced non-financial assets;
 • transactions of secondary income which shows the redistribution of income; and
 • acquisition and disposal of financial assets and liabilities
BOP consists of 3 main accounts:
 1. Current Account = Goods + Services + Primary Income + Secondary Income
 2. Capital Account
 3. Financial Account = Acquisition and disposal of Financial Assets + Liabilities
International transactions are recorded in the balance of payments on the basis of the double-entry principle used in business accounting, in which
each transaction gives rise to two offsetting entries of equal values so that in principle the resulting credit and debit entries always balance.
 IMBANGAN PEMBAYARAN
5.1  Imbangan Pembayaran
        Balance of Payments
BND Juta / Million
