122 123
BRUNEI DARUSSALAM STATISTICAL YEARBOOK 2025 BRUNEI DARUSSALAM STATISTICAL YEARBOOK 2025
 Nota Keterangan
Indeks Perdagangan Barangan Antarabangsa (IMTI) mengukur perubahan dalam nilai dan kuantiti unit. Indeks ini merupakan indeks
perangkaan yang menggambarkan tren, nilai unit dan volum eksport dan import barangan di Negara Brunei Darussalam dalam tempoh
tertentu.
IMTI disusun daripada nilai dan kuantiti Perangkaan Perdagangan Barangan Antarabangsa (IMTS). Sumber IMTS adalah berdasarkan data
import dan eksport yang diperolehi daripada Jabatan Kastam dan Eksais Diraja, Kementerian Kewangan dan Ekonomi melalui deklarasi
kastam, dan Jabatan Tenaga, Jabatan Perdana Menteri. Kewajaran tahun asas IMTI adalah 2015.
Penyusunan IMTI meliputi indeks seperti berikut:
i. Indeks Nilai Unit Eksport  mengukur perubahan dalam nilai unit barangan yang dieksport dari Negara Brunei Darussalam, termasuk eksport
semula. Nilai unit yang digunakan dalam pengiraan indeks adalah nilai unit barangan yang keluar secara fizikal melalui pelabuhan utama
eksport Negara Brunei Darussalam.
ii. Indeks Nilai Unit Import  digunakan sebagai indikator untuk mengukur perubahan dalam nilai unit barangan import ke Negara Brunei
Darussalam. Nilai unit import dinilaikan mengikut c.i.f. (cost, insurance and freight - kos, insurans dan pengangkutan).
iii. Indeks Volum Eksport  mengukur perubahan kuantiti barangan yang dieksport dari Negara Brunei Darussalam.
iv. Indeks Volum Import mengukur perubahan kuantiti barangan yang diimport ke Negara Brunei Darussalam.
v. Terma Indeks Perdagangan  mengukur nilai unit relatif eksport dari segi nilai unit import. Terma indeks perdagangan dikira berdasarkan
nisbah indeks nilai unit eksport ke indeks nilai unit import.
Explanatory Note
The International Merchandise Trade Index (IMTI) measures the changes in unit value and quantity. This index is a statistical index that reflects the
trends, unit value and volume of exports and imports of goods in Brunei Darussalam within a certain period of time.
The IMTI is compiled from the value and quantity of International Merchandise Trade Statistics (IMTS). The source of IMTS are based on the imports
and exports data submitted by the Royal Customs and Excise Department, Ministry of Finance and Economy through customs declarations, and the
Department of Energy, Prime Minister’s Office. The weight for IMTI base year is 2015.
The compilation of IMTI comprises of the following:
i.  Exports Unit Value Index measures changes in the unit values of exported goods from Brunei Darussalam, including re-exports. Unit value used in
the index computation is the unit value of goods that physically leave Brunei Darussalam’s main ports of export.
ii.  Imports Unit Value Index is used as an indicator to measure changes in unit values of imported goods into Brunei Darussalam. The unit value of
imports is valued at c.i.f. (cost, insurance and freight).
iii. Exports Volume Index measures the changes in the quantity of exported goods from Brunei Darussalam.
iv. Imports Volume Index measures the changes in the quantity of imported goods to Brunei Darussalam.
v. Terms of Trade Index measures the relative unit value of exports in terms of import unit value. The terms of trade index is calculated based on the
ratio of unit value index of exports to the unit value index of imports.
8
